course: dictionary
lesson: 7479
title: Pose: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Pose can be a verb (something you do) or a noun (a thing you can have). Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits.
explain: «She copies every photo pose she does.» A pose here is a way of standing for a photo, so pose is a noun. The clue is photo: people hold a pose when someone takes their picture.
explain: Pose can also mean to ask or cause something. A teacher can pose a question, and a problem can pose a threat. Here pose means to put something forward for someone to answer or deal with.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right one.
fact: Pose can be a verb: to pose means to stay still in a special position, for a photo or a picture.
fact: A pose is a way of standing or sitting, especially for a photo or drawing.
fact: To pose a question or a problem means to ask it or cause it.
fact: To pose as someone means to pretend to be them.
fact: Someone may pose as a friend online to trick you, so always check who people really are.
exercise: «She copies every photo pose she does.» What is a pose in this sentence? | *A way of standing for a photo | A kind of question | A loud noise | Something you buy in a shop
exercise: Miss Hughes says, «Let me pose a question about the planets.» What does pose mean here? | To fall over | *To ask or put forward | To pretend to be someone | To stay still for a photo
exercise: Ella says, «The stranger tried to pose as my cousin.» What does pose as mean? | *To pretend to be my cousin | To take a photo of my cousin | To draw my cousin | To ask my cousin a question
test: Sam says «strike a pose» means to hit something. What does it really mean? | To punch the air | *To stand in a special position, often for a photo | To write a letter | To run very fast
test: A stranger online tries to pose as a friend of yours. What should you do? | *Check who they really are before you trust them | Tell them your home address | Believe every message they send | Send them your password straight away
exam: Which sentence uses pose as a noun? | *Mum asked her to strike a pose for the photo | The bad weather will pose a problem for the walk | The teacher will pose a question to the class | Ella may pose as her cousin online
